A||N||13||WhiteFieroBlur||Calipers?||||8||
Z||000000||WhiteFieroBlur||06-27-2000||09:49 PM||||Well everyone tells me its the caliper but one guy says its not. Here is the problem.<P>I drive down the street and everything is fine. I keep going and the steering wheel starts to pull to the left and I let go of the wheel and the car goes right to the left so I have to keep the car to the right the whole time or I am gonna go into the left lane. The guy told me that its the caliper if I brake and it pulls to the left. But when I brake, I have total control of the car. It goes straight. it only pulls to the right when I drive. Soon the left tire starts to smell like its burning and I have to pull over and the brake feels spongy. I can smell the tire or something burning and if I touch the rims its too hot to touch.<BR>  So is it the calipers or what? I don't drive my car far, just down the street and back to work. I am too scared to go far till its fixed.<BR>||||reg||8
Z||000001||lawrence||06-27-2000||10:41 PM||||Sounds like a caliper to me.<P>Jack up the car and see if you can rotate the tire with your hands.  If there's a lot of resistance, then it's probably the caliper.<P>Then pull the wheel off and see if you can move the caliper on the sliders.  You will have to push the piston back into the bore.  If you can't do that, then either the piston is frozen or your brake line is blocked.<P>Good luck,<P>-L<BR> <A HREF="http://members.nccw.net/webe" TARGET=_blank>http://members.nccw.net/webe</A>  - WebElectric Magazine||||reg||1
Z||000002||-=shame=-||06-27-2000||11:01 PM||||OK. I've been fighting 1 caliper for three weeks now. They can be a serious pain. You must know which tire is getting hot. Thats yer problem, Chilton's books are best by FAR. That will walk you through swaping it out. I do suggest replacing the brake hose at the same time as the caliper, because it could really be either. Check my post New To Fiero a couple of good ideas, but a few to not do. Is it rear? And if so is it Auto or Manual? <P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||WhiteFieroBlur||06-28-2000||01:56 AM||||I know which tire it is, its the front left tire. Thats the one that gets hot and has the burnt smell to it. And I have a V6 standard 5 speed. I am not really a tire expert and I was gonna take it to a tire place for them to fix it but I asked around and its real expensive and I know that I can't ride around for too long like this without something seriously happening. is there a fix to make it stop getting hot and burning like temp.? or am I going to have to replace the caliper?||||reg||1
Z||000004||mbramble||06-28-2000||07:36 AM||||If it's the caliper, you are going to have to at least rebuild it.  Maybe even replace it.  I don't think there is any safe temporary fix.  Rebuilding is really rather simple and you can get a rebuild kit for both front wheels for less than 10 bucks.  If you don't have a shop manual, you might want to pick up a Haynes manual for the Fiero at your local auto parts store.  Not the best reference in the world but it will get you through a disassembly, rebuild, reinstall of the calipers, brake pads, rotors -- and many other routine maintenance and repair items.<P>There is information on both rebuilding and replacing calipers here.  I think it talks mostly about the rear wheels, but you can get an idea.  The front wheels are even easier because there is no emergency brake connection and the pistons are much simpler to remove and install.<BR> <A HREF="http://members.xoom.com/fierov6/OSG/brake-calipers.html" TARGET=_blank>http://members.xoom.com/fierov6/OSG/brake-calipers.html</A> <P>The Main Page is here: <A HREF="http://members.xoom.com/fierov6/OSG/osg.html" TARGET=_blank>http://members.xoom.com/fierov6/OSG/osg.html</A>   <BR>Look down in the Miscellaneous for brake pads, rotors and calipers.<P>You can do it!!  Get a mechanically inclined friend to give you a hand and save yourself a LOT of money.....||||reg||1
Z||000005||-=shame=-||06-28-2000||08:01 AM||||Yeah man! You can do it! If you go with NAPA or other namebrand parts a caliper and hose together could run $170. I got mine at an AutoZone discount parts totaling $65. There is a core charge on the caliper, between $60 and $90. <BR>The reason I asked if it were auto or manual was mine is auto, with the left rear caliper. Can't turn the tire then.<BR>Curious, what were you quoted on the job?||||reg||1
Z||000006||WhiteFieroBlur||06-28-2000||10:20 AM||||I called midas and they gave me a quote over the phone, he gave me a worse case senario if I messed up the brakes and rotor and everything and he said 300 dollars. I know I don't wanna do that. I called another place and they told me around 150 for everything. and this is just 1 tire. Midas wanted me to come in so they can check all my brakes first so they can tell me I need more than 1 wheel done  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">. But I am sure my step dad can do it himself with just buying the parts from autozone or something.  <BR>  thanx ||||reg||1
Z||000007||-=shame=-||06-29-2000||06:38 AM||||NOT Midas, they'll rape you!||||reg||4
Z||000008||WhiteFieroBlur||06-30-2000||04:45 PM||||I had my brakes and caliper changed on my car just today. I only cost 50 dollars for 1 caliper and brake bads on both sides. Hopefully everything well be better now. I almost forgot what its like to actually enjoy my fiero without worrying about my brakes. I have been driving it like a grandma for the past week. Its now time to take her back on the road and eat up cars :d||||reg||10
Z||000009||mbramble||06-30-2000||06:17 PM||||So, who did the work???<P>||||reg||1
Z||000010||WhiteFieroBlur||07-01-2000||12:43 AM||||well my step dad did the work, Its so easy to do, I can't believe they would charge so much like at midas to do it. ||||reg||1
Z||000011||mbramble||07-01-2000||08:43 AM||||Great!!  I was hoping you would say that.  And watching/helping him you should be able to do it the next time.  Doing your own work, with the help of family/friends when necessary will save you massive amounts of money over the years.  And, it's what this Forum is all about!!||||reg||1
Z||000012||beachbomb||07-01-2000||09:21 PM||||HI, i have a 1984 Indy Fiero, had the exact same problem a month ago, so i hade both front tires fixed(calipers and hoses), a week later the left rear did the same thing, so i had both rears done as well. Take it from me, have all 4 done at the same time(calipers and hoses) it will save you alot of time and frustration in the long run. Even though only one is bad now!..||||reg||14
Z||000013||WhiteFieroBlur||07-02-2000||03:02 AM||||we changed out both front brakes so it would balance out, does it still pull to the left on the back tires too, like the front ones?||||reg||1
